            "review_title": "Review at Com Tam Cali",
            "review_text": "Anika B\n3 contributions\n0\nExtremely Poor Customer Service\nFeb 2024 • Couples\nThis restaurant refused us service because of the color of our skin. I shouldn’t have been surprised, but when we travel I guess we should. \n\nOur group of 4 (American Black 53-63 yrs) were referred there by our tour guide. We walked in, a young girl (about 19) sat us at our table, then never came back until we flagged her down about 15 minutes later. We began to order and she immediately said we’re out of that. We said ok, and select several other dishes, including something very simple, spring rolls, she continued to say they were out of everything we requested. It was at this time we just decided to leave. \n\nOn our way out we noticed two of our tour mates (white Canadian) they ordered items similar to ours and were promptly served.\n\nIt’s so disappointing and disgustingly awful that people continue to have such deep prejudice against human beings they have never met and most certainly never see again, simply because of the color of their skin. It’s unfortunate and tragic. \n\nI hope this wards off any other of my fellow travelers from eating at this establishment, because people like that should not remain in business.\nRead more\nWritten February 27, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
