            "review_text": "Frankie B\nPerth, Australia295 contributions\n0\nGreat cafe with inexpensive nourishing meals\nFeb 2016 • Couples\nIn an area almost opposite the 5 Star EASTIN GRAND HOTEL near the airport it was great to find this café with good Vietnamese food. \n\nWe were the only \"foreigners\" in a very popular eatery, so we knew the food had to be good, I had the two HUGE spring rolls, delicious and very filling! Cost USD 1.88. My partner had the Pork Belly with the famous Broken Rise. (Approx USD4)\n\nA great alternative to the very much more expensive meals in our hotel.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten March 1, 2016",
